1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:03,340
Let me share a simple message tip for iPhone users.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,000
It’s really useful, do give it a try.

3
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:10,340
To get more helpful videos like this, subscribe to the channel right away and stay tuned.

4
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:12,360
I will keep uploading great content.

5
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:16,200
Now, let's see how it works. Open the Messages app on your phone.

6
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:22,400
Select the contact you want to message, and you can send invisible messages just like this.

7
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:30,200
They will receive it the same way, hidden until they scratch over it to read.

8
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:33,550
It is a very simple and handy tip.

9
00:00:33,550 --> 00:00:42,360
Here's how to do it: select the contact and type your message.

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:48,380
Instead of tapping the send button, long-press on it.

11
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:51,575
You will see three or four effect options appear.

12
00:00:51,645 --> 00:00:57,485
You can use any of them—I'll cover the invisible effect at the end.

13
00:00:57,535 --> 00:01:04,700
The first option at the top is "Slam." If you select Slam and hit send, it delivers with a slam effect.

14
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:11,470
If you pick the second option, "Loud," it sends with an animated notification effect.

15
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:17,280
The third option applies another subtle visual effect.

16
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:24,000
The fourth one is "Invisible Ink," which we talked about earlier.

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,700
Select "Send with Invisible Ink" and tap Send.

18
00:01:30,940 --> 00:01:35,640
The recipient receives the message hidden under a digital scratch layer.

19
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:40,660
They can simply swipe or scratch over the bubble to read it.

20
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:42,520
Isn't that a neat trick?

21
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:44,480
Follow along for more useful tips like this!

22
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:49,640
Share this video with others so more people learn about these features.

23
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:52,120
See you again soon with another new topic!

